WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our first guest tonight
is an Oscar-nominated,

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.971
Golden Globe-winning actress
you know from films like

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:08.474
"American Hustle" and "Vice", as
well as HBO's "Sharp Objects".

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:11.243
She stars in "Dear Evan Hansen",
which is in theaters

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:13.546
September 24th.
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.883
-I mean, most people think
that I'm... [clicks tongue]

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:21.321
not that cool of a person, so
nobody wants to hear from me.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.392
-Well, it --

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:30.563
That's what most people think.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.099
Sounds like most people
don't know you very well.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.368
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.803
-Didn't know Connor, either.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.373
They never bothered.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.675
-Please welcome back to the show
Amy Adams.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.844
Hello, Amy.
It's always good to see you.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.712
-Hi, Seth! It's good to
see you, too.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:48.547
How are you?
-I am wonderful.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:51.918
This is now the third time I've
been lucky enough to check in

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:55.521
with you remotely, and I want to
just see where we're going

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.057
as far as hobbies.
I feel like early on,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.392
we were messing around
with stringed instruments.

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:01.794
Felt like maybe...
-Yeah.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.796
-...We abandoned that one.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.631
-I did. I did aban--
Well...

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.200
Yeah, did. Yeah, I didn't --
-OK, thank you.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.168
It felt like you were going to
maybe say no,

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:12.004
but then you came -- you found
your way to the truth.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.740
-I did. I was going to maybe
baby lie on that one,

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.310
and then I thought,
"No, the truth is easier."

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.245
-Yeah.
-Then we talked a little about

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.948
dancing -- I feel like
your daughter really has

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.849
the skills that maybe made
you think,

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.618
"She's my daughter. I probably
have the skills, too."

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.052
How's the dancing going?

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.022
-Dancing's going okay.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.825
I had been dancing for a film
that we'll talk about later,

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.595
but I thought, "Okay,
I'm going to get into

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.163
this TikTok thing."
-Very wise. Very wise.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.366
-Which is mortifying for her.
I'm not on TikTok,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.635
and so the only TikTok dance
that I have

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.005
even partially learned is
from the Applebee's commercial.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.640
Because I -- [ Laughs ]
I don't know

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.108
if you know
that song "Fancy Like".

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.178
-Yes. Walker Hayes.
Yes. We had him here doing it.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.446
Yes.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.414
-I'm always behind on
everything,

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:58.651
so I actually thought that was
just an Applebee's commercial.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.186
-Right.
-So.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:03.656
-That really is -- you're right.
That's when you know your age,

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.826
is when you -- you think
it's from the commercial.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.395
-That Applebee's jingle
is really catchy.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.397
Yeah, but the dance
is catchy, too,

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.266
so that's the only one
I've actually learned.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.134
-Can you? Can you, from
a sitting position,

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.637
is there any of that
you can show us,

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.306
as far as what
that TikTok dance is?

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.274
-I can try.
-OK, great.

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:26.712
-OK. ♪ Yeah, we're fancy like
Applebee's on a date night ♪

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:29.916
♪ Got a Bourbon Street steak
and an Oreo shake ♪

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.851
♪ Got the whipped cream on
the top, too ♪

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:35.587
♪ Two straws, one check,
yeah, I got you ♪

00:02:35.587 --> 00:02:37.523
It's -- What's happening down
here is just as good.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.325
So you can just --
-[ Laughs ] Okay.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.827
Will you just send us
a tape of that later?

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.595
And we'll marry the two.

00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:45.598
-Sure, sure.
-How now --

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.366
Your daughter is how old?
-That's not embarrassing at all

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:48.767
for my daughter,
what I just did.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.470
-Well, that's what I was
going to ask.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.004
How is -- How is she responding?

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.806
By the way,
they say you probably --

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.676
it's not safe
to do a TikTok dance

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.812
if you're old enough to have
a row of vinyl behind you.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.514
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:05.284
-This is probably true.
This is probably true.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:09.222
-How does she feel
when you do your dances?

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.757
-I think the word
she uses is "cringe."

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.626
-Oh, no.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.729
-But she's patient with me.
I've been embarrassing her

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:20.299
for 11 great years,
and, you know, more to come.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.567
-Think you have way much more to
come.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.236
-Yeah.
-This is really cool.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.705
I know that you were,
like many people,

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:29.375
a huge fan of "Dear Evan Hansen"
when it was on Broadway.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.777
It must be so nice
to be involved in this project

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.645
now that it's on film.

00:03:33.645 --> 00:03:36.682
-It's amazing. I'm so honored
to be a part of this.

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.185
It's got such beautiful
messaging,

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.887
beautiful, talented actors,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.956
and again, I'm just honored
to be a part of it.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.692
Broadway and stage
is my first love,

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.362
so it's nice to get to
honor it in this way.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:52.498
-I'm sure people are often very
nervous and excited to meet you,

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:56.369
but this was the reverse, when
you got to work with Ben Platt

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:59.972
because you'd been so blown away
by him on stage. Is that right?

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:03.476
-Yeah, I was -- I was very --

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.244
I -- It's weird
because it's intimidated,

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.981
but it's only by his talent
because his -- as a human,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:11.017
he's just so gracious
and wonderful.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:14.687
But yeah, it was -- it was --
to, like, sing in front of him

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.655
at our first table read
was terrifying.

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:19.725
But again, he's so gracious.
I mean, because he shows you

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.727
what's possible,
and then you sing,

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.964
and then it's what you do,
which is different, you know?

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.832
-He shows you what's possible
for Ben Platt.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.502
I think that is maybe a fair way
to put it.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.971
-That's fair.
-Did you enjoy getting to

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:34.239
spend time with, you know,
what must be --

00:04:34.239 --> 00:04:35.641
you know, obviously,
this is a show where

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:38.544
a lot of the cast
are played by younger people.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.946
-Yeah, I -- I mean,
I say that --

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:43.382
that sounded doubtful.

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.951
I love them.
But again, I get so excited,

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:49.355
and Kaitlyn Dever was someone
that I had been sort of...

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.124
online pursuing.
I don't like the "S" word,

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.860
but I was sort of getting
to know all about her online,

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.496
and really,
really love her work.

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.132
She's a beautiful singer.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.133
And then we met.
I sort of gushed all over her.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.603
And then we did have
some musical things in common,

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:07.240
so then I thought, you know,
"I'm just as cool as her,"

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.774
which I'm not, so.

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:11.076
-Did you bring that back
and report that to your daughter

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.546
as evidence
that you're a cool young person?

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:16.082
-Yeah, I would say --
Kaitlyn knows who Brett is,

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:19.018
so I must be cool.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:22.588
-And then did her
just, like, eyes glass over?

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.457
She -- You know what?
She's at this place

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.692
where she's actually
really kind to me about it.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.193
Like, she can see my struggle

00:05:28.193 --> 00:05:31.864
and she kind of --
she's patient with it.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.999
-I think that means you're a
good mom, that you've raised

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.535
such an empathetic daughter
who feels so deeply for

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:39.305
her cringy --
her cringy mom's feelings.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.539
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:43.109
-Yeah, I'd like --
I'm going to take that as a win.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.277
-So this is -- we talked about
this a little bit last time

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.046
you were here. I'm sure
it's further down the line now,

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.414
but you're doing "Disenchanted",

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:51.283
which is a sequel to
"Enchanted".

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:54.954
This is a very, you know --
a long gap between the two.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.990
Has it been just a delight
to return to the character?

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.226
-It has been wonderful.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.761
That's the film
I was talking about,

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.096
that I was training
and dancing again for.

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:06.666
It's been wonderful.
She's -- Returning to Giselle,

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:09.602
she's such a positive attitude
and so much energy

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.904
and really always tries
to see the best in people,

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:15.240
and that's something I always
try to remind myself to do,

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.044
so it's nice to return to her.
Different.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.946
-I also -- I feel like you took
on a hobby that, like,

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:22.548
unlike learning
to play the cello,

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.417
was one that
you could accomplish.

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:27.152
It's one for other people
to accomplish.

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:29.355
And I'm actually -- when I heard
that you were doing it,

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.956
I'm like, "I think that sounds
pretty good."

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:34.227
You started binge-watching
"Murder, She Wrote".

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:37.396
-I did.
I love "Murder, She Wrote",

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.098
and next on the list is
"Matlock".

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:42.468
Maybe I'll get Kaitlyn Dever
to watch it with me.

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.669
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.738
There's a reason.
We'll talk about it sometime.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.407
I know. But when I did -- when
I used to do dinner theater,

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:51.576
I didn't have cable,
and so the only thing on

00:06:51.576 --> 00:06:53.645
when I got home at night --
it was like 11 or 12 --

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:55.181
was "Matlock"
and "Murder, She Wrote".

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:58.284
So I'm now revisiting those.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:00.987
-I think it's a really nice
bookend

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.722
that we started
talking about TikTok

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.790
and we ended
talking about "Matlock".

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.091
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:07.659
-Kind of. Well, yeah.

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:10.763
That's a little peek inside
there, Seth.

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.632
-Hey, it's always so great
to see you.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.467
Next time -- I'm feeling very
confident next time

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.370
is going to be in person.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.538
-Yes, 100% will make
that happen.

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:20.539
-All right, great,
thanks so much, Amy.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.041
-And then you can
see the feet.

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.842
-Oh man, you better --
don't oversell it

00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:25.144
because we are going to --
-OK, OK.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.212
-We're going to take a real look
at these feet. [ Laughs ]

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:28.714
-OK, fair enough.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.050
-"Dear Evan Hansen" is in
theaters September 24th.

